DirectXShaderCompiler v1.9.2609 (commit 01b62ad47db7dee3dd33f90e7339cf9e860b3f93): build dxcompiler.dll with MinGW-w64 (llvm-mingw).

Taken from DirectXShaderCompiler pull request #8265, "[MinGW] Test building on different platforms", by Raed Rizqie
(https://github.com/microsoft/DirectXShaderCompiler/pull/8265, head c1d55772d52b54a28c69f713964295d7a407da7f, five commits of
2026-03-11; closed unmerged on 2026-10-29), offered to the project under its own licence (University of Illinois/NCSA, LICENSE.TXT).
Applied for BCD in November 2026 with two changes:
  - left out: the PR's second StringRef.h hunk, which removes the is_nothrow_constructible specialisations that v1.9.2609 already
    skips under libc++ (_LIBCPP_VERSION), the C++ library llvm-mingw uses (its first, #include <cstdint>, is kept);
  - replaced: the PR defines MS_SUPPORT_VARIABLE_LANGOPTS for MinGW in tools/clang/CMakeLists.txt, which turns DXC's fixed HLSL
    language options into clang's variable ones with C defaults (the DLL then read HLSL as C: "unknown type name 'float4'"). BCD keeps
    the options fixed and gives MinGW the out-of-class definitions LLVM's Unix build already has (tools/clang/lib/Basic/LangOptions.cpp).
See build/dxc-win/BCD-SOURCE.txt and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. Applied by tools/build-dxcompiler.sh with `git apply`.

